{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":true},"context":"rlc-circuit-calculator UI copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer","detected_language":"tl","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"rlc-circuit-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer","keys":["rlc-circuit-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer"],"locale":"fil","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"Para sa modelong serye, Q = ω₀L/R at ang bandwidth ay R/(ZXQPH0000QXZπL). Para sa modelong paralelo, Q = R/(ω₀L) at ang bandwidth ay ZXQPH0001QXZ/(ZXQPH0002QXZπRC).","record_id":"0d6007a388fd0a1ab34aa1c5c0df2877a5342ed3c740b30ee25cf4d73bc5d4b9","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"40843674935","seconds":1.0360301591249765,"source":"For the series model, Q = ω₀L/R and bandwidth is R/(2πL). For the parallel model, Q = R/(ω₀L) and bandwidth is 1/(2πRC). These are ideal single-resonance relationships.","source_commit":"e1f72394198c1a94fce448ea14cd79b496701273","source_hash":"d929113d31b49cd67fa0b70f4d3ec5403c3e4e89c98b4fcab359fb6074436c8a","status":"machine-draft","translation":"Para sa modelong serye, Q = ω₀L/R at ang bandwidth ay R/(2πL). Para sa modelong paralelo, Q = R/(ω₀L) at ang bandwidth ay 1/(2πRC).","truncated":false,"warnings":[]}
